 "address": "Zeemanlaboratorium, Plantage Muidergracht 4 / Roetersstraat (1921-1923, rijksmonument 518497): red-brick physics laboratory, two tall storeys of white-framed grouped windows over a striped (street) or stone (canal) plinth, a stone head band under a plain parapet; entrance risalit with a raised parapet and the name plaque; a modern glazed/concrete-frame infill bay at the east end",
